WEBVTT

00:00:03.870 --> 00:00:05.400
Kaito Daimon:

00:00:05.400 --> 00:00:07.810
The possibility of Phi-Brain,
which could lead

00:00:07.810 --> 00:00:10.700
to the Puzzle of God,
lies hidden within him.

00:00:10.700 --> 00:00:13.930
I would ask that you
fight the Givers of the

00:00:13.930 --> 00:00:16.590
POG as a Solver with
the title of Einstein.

00:00:16.590 --> 00:00:18.700
The one who desired this barrier
to be released

00:00:18.700 --> 00:00:20.070
was Baron Kaidou!

00:00:20.070 --> 00:00:22.210
Baron Kaidou is the
school principal, right?

00:00:23.720 --> 00:00:26.040
This puzzle wants to be solved!

00:00:30.770 --> 00:00:32.010
Solved it.

00:00:50.600 --> 00:00:52.910
Kimi no nounai e to shinnyuu
Gonna infiltrate your brain

00:00:52.910 --> 00:00:55.640
Nemutteru suki ni baby, open the gate
While you're sleeping, baby, open the gate

00:00:55.640 --> 00:00:57.490
Fukuzatsusugi security
Too-complicated security

00:00:57.490 --> 00:01:00.230
Kakusareru to abakitakunaru
When something's hidden, it makes me want to expose it

00:01:00.230 --> 00:01:04.740
Barabara ni chirabatte iru password o hiroiatsume
I'll gather up those loose, scattered passwords

00:01:04.740 --> 00:01:09.450
Kakushin ni sematte yuku, sono shoutai o misete
And approach the core, so show me that true form

00:01:09.450 --> 00:01:11.670
Kantan ni clear dekinai
I can't clear it easily

00:01:11.670 --> 00:01:14.320
Saki nante motto yomenai
Can read what lies ahead even less

00:01:14.320 --> 00:01:16.330
Kaidoku fukanou smile
A smile that can't be deciphered

00:01:16.330 --> 00:01:18.630
Kiken na puzzle
A dangerous puzzle

00:01:18.630 --> 00:01:20.570
Lock sareteta door aru nara
If there's a door that's been locked

00:01:20.570 --> 00:01:23.390
Zutto tataite miru beki, kaza-ana hiraku wa
You must keep striking it, a crack will open

00:01:23.390 --> 00:01:27.890
Eien ni hodokenai nazo nanka wa nai
No mystery remains unsolved forever

00:01:27.890 --> 00:01:30.190
Makiokosu, it's a supernova!
It's forming, it's a supernova!

00:01:30.190 --> 00:01:34.880
Tobikiri shigekiteki na hirameki o agemashou
I will give you thoroughly stimulating insight

00:01:34.880 --> 00:01:37.100
Misskey-misskey la-tu-ma

00:01:37.100 --> 00:01:39.440
Yume no naka, it's a supernova!
In the middle of a dream, it's a supernova!

00:01:39.440 --> 00:01:42.070
Watashi wa, sou, brain diver
I am, yes, a brain diver

00:01:42.070 --> 00:01:47.960
Kimi ga sagashimotometeru kotae ni nareru made
Until I become familiar with the answer you seek

00:01:50.620 --> 00:01:53.640
Brain diver

00:01:55.370 --> 00:01:58.440
Brain diver

00:02:03.810 --> 00:02:06.960
The Melancholy of a Boy Genius

00:02:09.360 --> 00:02:11.230
Just explain yourself already!

00:02:11.830 --> 00:02:14.980
Upperclassman Jikukawa,
why does this thing

00:02:14.980 --> 00:02:17.810
you gave me receive puzzles from the POG?

00:02:17.810 --> 00:02:22.100
Why indeed? I don't
really get it, either.

00:02:22.100 --> 00:02:23.580
You playin' dumb?

00:02:23.580 --> 00:02:26.080
Principal! You say somethin', too!

00:02:27.430 --> 00:02:29.790
Makin' me solve these
damn deadly puzzles...!

00:02:31.100 --> 00:02:34.030
How are you two involved with the POG?

00:02:34.030 --> 00:02:35.660
What do you know?

00:02:35.660 --> 00:02:38.310
That's a difficult question to answer...

00:02:38.310 --> 00:02:41.570
It's nothing for you to be
concerned about, Kaito Daimon.

00:02:41.570 --> 00:02:42.300
Huh?

00:02:42.830 --> 00:02:45.180
What kinda nonsense are you talkin' now?!

00:02:45.180 --> 00:02:47.010
I am not concerned about it, either.

00:02:47.010 --> 00:02:49.140
Quit tryin' to fool me! I...!

00:02:49.140 --> 00:02:50.680
That car.

00:02:50.680 --> 00:02:54.040
The car you so kindly destroyed was an

00:02:54.040 --> 00:02:56.690
extremely rare classic, one
of only two in the world.

00:02:57.730 --> 00:03:01.090
Well, that crew-cut bastard
used a dirty trick, and-

00:03:01.090 --> 00:03:03.660
Releasing the prize in one piece.

00:03:03.660 --> 00:03:06.840
THAT is what constitutes having
solved a puzzle. Very well.

00:03:06.840 --> 00:03:07.770
You sonofa-

00:03:07.770 --> 00:03:09.540
Let's put it at 20 million yen.

00:03:09.540 --> 00:03:10.350
Twenty mil-?!

00:03:10.350 --> 00:03:12.210
That is a bargain.

00:03:12.660 --> 00:03:17.090
Your continuing to solve
Philosopher's Puzzles for us

00:03:17.090 --> 00:03:19.170
will let this end without casualties.

00:03:22.880 --> 00:03:24.810
Ah, Kaito!

00:03:24.810 --> 00:03:26.360
My apologies!

00:03:28.900 --> 00:03:31.140
This is Einstein...

00:03:31.820 --> 00:03:34.300
What relation would he
have to the principal?

00:03:35.510 --> 00:03:37.060
Kaito, wait!

00:03:40.980 --> 00:03:42.640
What will you do, Kaito?

00:03:42.640 --> 00:03:45.870
If you get another invitation
to solve a Philosopher's Puzzle...

00:03:46.150 --> 00:03:47.420
Will you go solve it?

00:03:47.770 --> 00:03:49.620
Like hell I will!

00:03:50.320 --> 00:03:52.010
Stupid Philosopher's Puzzles.

00:03:52.010 --> 00:03:53.470
I know, right?

00:03:53.470 --> 00:03:56.260
Quitting is the way to
go. It's way dangerous.

00:03:56.260 --> 00:03:57.770
That's a good answer.

00:04:01.770 --> 00:04:04.920
I'm glad you've realized
that puzzles are worthless.

00:04:04.920 --> 00:04:06.100
Who are you supposed to be?

00:04:06.670 --> 00:04:11.180
I'm Cubik Galois, a second-year at
Root Gakuen Middle School.

00:04:11.180 --> 00:04:13.480
Oh, and I hold the title of Edison.

00:04:13.990 --> 00:04:15.340
Title?

00:04:15.340 --> 00:04:17.310
Meaning, you're a genius?

00:04:17.720 --> 00:04:20.930
Puzzles aren't meant for geniuses.

00:04:20.930 --> 00:04:23.820
There are other things that we must do.

00:04:24.320 --> 00:04:25.860
"Things we must do"?

00:04:25.860 --> 00:04:28.080
This way. My friends waiting.

00:04:28.720 --> 00:04:30.310
The hell is he?

00:04:30.310 --> 00:04:31.360
Hurry up!

00:04:31.360 --> 00:04:34.390
Looks like a bother if
we don't do as he says...

00:04:39.970 --> 00:04:41.950
Everyone, sorry for the wait.

00:04:41.950 --> 00:04:43.620
I brought Kaito with me.

00:04:43.620 --> 00:04:45.130
Where are your friends?

00:04:45.510 --> 00:04:49.260
This is Mr. Poincaré Conjecture and
Mr. Riemann Hypothesis.

00:04:49.260 --> 00:04:51.370
We've been friends a long time.

00:04:52.340 --> 00:04:54.390
I don't understand what he's saying.

00:04:55.920 --> 00:04:57.700
The world of mathematics
holds many mysteries,

00:04:57.700 --> 00:05:01.620
far greater than "puzzles" invented by man.

00:05:01.620 --> 00:05:02.740
For example...

00:05:03.750 --> 00:05:04.700
What?

00:05:04.700 --> 00:05:08.550
1, 12, 123, and so on:

00:05:08.550 --> 00:05:10.990
multiply each by 9 and
add ascending positive integers...

00:05:10.990 --> 00:05:15.370
The result is a repeated
unit of 1. Always.

00:05:15.600 --> 00:05:16.770
Huh?

00:05:18.330 --> 00:05:20.670
Y..You're right! That's weird.

00:05:20.790 --> 00:05:23.980
Doing nothing but puzzles every day...

00:05:23.980 --> 00:05:27.260
You think such things
are allowed us geniuses?

00:05:27.940 --> 00:05:31.820
We must use our minds for
the benefit of others.

00:05:31.820 --> 00:05:35.060
Kaito, assist me in my research.

00:05:35.620 --> 00:05:38.350
Yeah, right. Let's go, Nonoha.

00:05:38.780 --> 00:05:41.400
Okay. Well, see you later, Cubik.

00:05:51.320 --> 00:05:54.430
Mr. President. Do you have a moment?

00:05:54.800 --> 00:05:57.160
Ah, now's no good. Sorry.

00:05:57.960 --> 00:06:00.200
LISTEN to me once in a while!

00:06:00.200 --> 00:06:02.000
More to the point, the student council-

00:06:02.000 --> 00:06:03.340
Uh-oh.

00:06:03.880 --> 00:06:05.850
Persistent, aren't you?

00:06:06.300 --> 00:06:07.390
I'm just-

00:06:07.390 --> 00:06:10.160
Not you, Chieno.

00:06:11.870 --> 00:06:14.680
That kid really is persistent.

00:06:15.240 --> 00:06:16.440
Say, Kaito!

00:06:16.440 --> 00:06:17.690
Don't be followin' me.

00:06:17.980 --> 00:06:20.300
You won't do puzzles anymore, right?

00:06:21.200 --> 00:06:23.390
That's got nothin' to do with you!

00:06:35.120 --> 00:06:37.230
Hey! What is this?!

00:06:37.230 --> 00:06:39.240
A charm to keep puzzles away.

00:06:40.610 --> 00:06:42.750
I invented it just for you.

00:06:44.160 --> 00:06:47.480
"Invented"? That's Edison, all right.

00:06:47.480 --> 00:06:48.700
I don't need it!

00:06:52.840 --> 00:06:54.230
I can't... get it off!

00:06:55.690 --> 00:06:58.050
You will thank me soon enough.

00:07:02.660 --> 00:07:05.480
Bastard! Get this thing offa me!

00:07:06.320 --> 00:07:09.400
Yeah, I wonder if a lot
of geniuses are weirdoes.

00:07:10.460 --> 00:07:12.530
Gammon, and Cubik...

00:07:13.310 --> 00:07:14.360
And you.

00:07:20.150 --> 00:07:22.260
It won't come off.

00:07:22.260 --> 00:07:25.540
But having TWO bracelets is
stylish, don't you think?

00:07:25.540 --> 00:07:27.450
You really don't care, do you?

00:07:27.450 --> 00:07:29.210
I'm glad that you care for it.

00:07:34.010 --> 00:07:34.880
Wow.

00:07:34.880 --> 00:07:36.620
I told you, don't follow me!

00:07:36.620 --> 00:07:38.600
You'll be cryin' when this is over!

00:07:56.870 --> 00:07:59.460
It looks like he gave up. Cubik.

00:07:59.460 --> 00:08:02.560
Lately, I'm gettin' mixed up
with nothin' but weirdoes!

00:08:04.130 --> 00:08:05.460
Aah, shut up!

00:08:06.360 --> 00:08:08.460
It's not an invitation, is it?

00:08:08.460 --> 00:08:09.170
Beats me.

00:08:11.700 --> 00:08:12.560
It's a puzzle.

00:08:13.130 --> 00:08:15.180
A puzzle like this,
I'll solve in a flash!

00:08:22.280 --> 00:08:23.140
Is something wrong?

00:08:25.080 --> 00:08:29.040
My head hurts when I try to think.

00:08:29.960 --> 00:08:31.700
Because of THIS, huh?

00:08:31.700 --> 00:08:33.570
What is this thing?

00:08:34.030 --> 00:08:35.820
Hey! What is this?!

00:08:36.160 --> 00:08:38.080
A charm to keep puzzles away.

00:08:38.610 --> 00:08:40.540
These numbers... Oh.

00:08:41.130 --> 00:08:42.610
This is a message.

00:08:42.610 --> 00:08:44.350
The meaning of each number is...

00:08:45.020 --> 00:08:46.790
Hey. You okay, Kaito?

00:08:46.790 --> 00:08:50.090
Each of these numbers
represents a letter.

00:08:50.510 --> 00:08:51.920
Gammon!

00:08:51.920 --> 00:08:55.550
Well, well! A puzzle like
THIS is giving you trouble?

00:08:56.240 --> 00:08:59.050
The numbers run through
the alphabet in order.

00:08:59.050 --> 00:09:03.060
01 is A, 02 is B. In other words!

00:09:03.340 --> 00:09:06.400
Replace these numbers with letters and...

00:09:06.400 --> 00:09:09.470
Oh my, how strange!

00:09:09.470 --> 00:09:11.030
One, two...

00:09:11.030 --> 00:09:14.070
"The Center Bldg Roof Top"!

00:09:14.070 --> 00:09:16.510
The answer lies at the top
of the Center Building!

00:09:16.510 --> 00:09:18.290
This has got nothing to do with you!

00:09:20.170 --> 00:09:22.620
The prize will be mine!

00:09:22.620 --> 00:09:24.100
Prize! Prize! Prize! Prize!

00:09:31.700 --> 00:09:33.130
May I help the next person, please?

00:09:34.880 --> 00:09:36.650
Who is this?

00:09:36.720 --> 00:09:38.720
So, are you POG?

00:09:39.080 --> 00:09:42.200
By day, I am head of the
Urban Development Unit.

00:09:42.200 --> 00:09:44.570
After 5:00, I am POG.

00:09:44.570 --> 00:09:48.220
I have played these two
roles for 35 years.

00:09:49.120 --> 00:09:51.180
You're a unit head and POG?

00:09:51.180 --> 00:09:54.190
My subordinates call me
Mr. Urban Development.

00:09:54.510 --> 00:09:56.600
Bastard! That hurts!

00:09:56.600 --> 00:09:59.810
I've devoted my life toward
urban development.

00:09:59.160 --> 00:10:00.660
L..Let go! Ow!

00:09:59.810 --> 00:10:01.660
If there were a building
coverage ratio for love,

00:10:01.660 --> 00:10:04.650
that which I have given
this city would be 100%.

00:10:04.650 --> 00:10:06.690
And all for this moment.

00:10:06.690 --> 00:10:10.500
Our beloved city shall today be complete.

00:10:10.500 --> 00:10:14.790
The Solvers shall be Kaito Daimon
and Gammon Sakanoue.

00:10:16.310 --> 00:10:20.270
The prize that I have sealed
has been entrusted to you.

00:10:20.270 --> 00:10:22.810
However, if you do not
solve the puzzle...

00:10:23.850 --> 00:10:26.090
This city shall be blown up.

00:10:26.090 --> 00:10:26.760
Huh?

00:10:26.760 --> 00:10:27.810
Blown up, you say?!

00:10:28.350 --> 00:10:29.640
What the heck?

00:10:29.640 --> 00:10:31.690
Didn't you give your all to build it?

00:10:32.010 --> 00:10:33.940
That is precisely why.

00:10:43.290 --> 00:10:46.100
You have only 16 minutes.

00:10:46.100 --> 00:10:48.440
Very well, start the puzzle.

00:10:48.440 --> 00:10:49.670
Sudoku, huh?

00:10:49.930 --> 00:10:53.840
Use the vowels next to the
numbers to find the keyword.

00:10:53.840 --> 00:10:57.420
That will be the key to the last stage.

00:10:57.740 --> 00:10:59.760
A sudoku like this is no-

00:11:02.480 --> 00:11:04.780
Damn! Again?!

00:11:06.060 --> 00:11:08.930
Oh? Is it that difficult?

00:11:09.880 --> 00:11:13.520
No! When I try to solve
it, my head hurts!

00:11:13.520 --> 00:11:17.570
That bracelet blocks his thoughts
when he tries to solve a puzzle.

00:11:27.890 --> 00:11:30.290
Cubik! What are you doing here?

00:11:37.950 --> 00:11:41.660
I used this to get a look
at the problem, too.

00:11:41.660 --> 00:11:43.200
Simple, wasn't it?

00:11:43.200 --> 00:11:44.450
Stay outta this!

00:11:44.450 --> 00:11:46.650
You a student at our school?!

00:11:45.940 --> 00:11:47.420
Yes, a second-year.

00:11:47.420 --> 00:11:50.580
An upperclassman?! Forgive my rudeness!

00:11:50.580 --> 00:11:51.840
In middle school.

00:11:51.840 --> 00:11:53.850
Why didn't you say so, bastard?!

00:11:54.140 --> 00:11:56.460
Sir, show me the problem.

00:11:58.700 --> 00:12:00.420
What are you...?

00:12:03.030 --> 00:12:04.240
Some hints are disappearing!

00:12:04.710 --> 00:12:05.530
What'd you say?!

00:12:05.530 --> 00:12:06.240
No way!

00:12:06.550 --> 00:12:08.860
I made it more difficult.

00:12:08.860 --> 00:12:12.040
True, the problem remains intact.

00:12:12.040 --> 00:12:13.980
Well done.

00:12:13.980 --> 00:12:17.130
"Puzzles" are little
more than this, anyway.

00:12:18.820 --> 00:12:21.590
Do you know what you've done, asshole?!

00:12:22.030 --> 00:12:24.730
If you can solve it, then fine.

00:12:24.730 --> 00:12:28.100
But if you admit that
puzzles are worthless,

00:12:28.100 --> 00:12:30.640
accept the things that a
genius should do, then-

00:12:29.570 --> 00:12:30.640
Solved it!

00:12:33.870 --> 00:12:35.360
I solved it.

00:12:35.360 --> 00:12:36.560
Me, too.

00:12:37.880 --> 00:12:38.790
Let's go.

00:12:38.790 --> 00:12:39.780
Go where?

00:12:41.440 --> 00:12:45.810
Um, I sure wish you'd tell me
the answer to the puzzle.

00:12:45.810 --> 00:12:46.990
Yeah...

00:12:46.990 --> 00:12:47.970
Can't be bothered.

00:12:49.350 --> 00:12:50.690
Listen up.

00:12:51.600 --> 00:12:55.210
A is 1 and 6.
So, 16.

00:12:55.210 --> 00:12:58.770
I is 1. U is
1 and 8, so 18.

00:12:58.770 --> 00:13:00.750
E is 1 and 1,
so 11.

00:13:01.030 --> 00:13:09.410
A         I         U         E

00:13:01.460 --> 00:13:04.590
Line the numbers up to the
corresponding letter and...

00:13:05.480 --> 00:13:06.430
P-

00:13:06.430 --> 00:13:07.230
P-A-

00:13:07.230 --> 00:13:08.240
P-A-R-

00:13:08.240 --> 00:13:09.090
P-A-R-K!

00:13:09.600 --> 00:13:10.720
PARK!

00:13:11.030 --> 00:13:12.920
Like, an outdoor park!

00:13:12.920 --> 00:13:14.780
So, the way to solve sudoku is...?

00:13:14.780 --> 00:13:15.980
Give it your all.

00:13:15.980 --> 00:13:17.080
Huh?

00:13:22.510 --> 00:13:26.420
<i>What do you think? A
beautiful park, isn't it?</i>

00:13:26.420 --> 00:13:28.460
Look, hurry up and give us the problem.

00:13:28.460 --> 00:13:34.340
<i>When making this park,
I hid 16 numbers somewhere within it.</i>

00:13:34.340 --> 00:13:39.030
<i>Find all the numbers and enter them correctly
within these blanks.</i>

00:13:39.030 --> 00:13:42.260
<i>Also, please be aware that the bomb</i>

00:13:42.260 --> 00:13:44.050
<i>is now located directly beneath you.</i>

00:13:44.240 --> 00:13:46.110
<i>That is all. Now then, if you please.</i>

00:13:46.800 --> 00:13:48.460
Huh? That's it?!

00:13:48.460 --> 00:13:52.260
<i>The city blown up, destroyed,
reduced to rubble...</i>

00:13:52.450 --> 00:13:56.020
That is the ultimate city,
which I had planned.

00:13:56.020 --> 00:14:00.390
City streets with my name as a Giver
forever carved into them!

00:14:02.360 --> 00:14:04.280
Sixteen numbers...

00:14:04.450 --> 00:14:07.780
Even if we find them, what
rule do we use to enter them?

00:14:08.960 --> 00:14:09.810
Kaito?

00:14:10.820 --> 00:14:12.160
This 5?

00:14:12.490 --> 00:14:14.680
No, it's 12-sided, so it's 12.

00:14:15.910 --> 00:14:17.160
Correct!

00:14:17.460 --> 00:14:19.450
The number appeared.

00:14:19.450 --> 00:14:22.440
All we can do is hunt around for numbers.

00:14:22.440 --> 00:14:24.550
Look, there's no time. Hurry!

00:14:24.550 --> 00:14:25.070
Okay!

00:14:25.070 --> 00:14:26.420
Don't act all bossy!

00:14:30.430 --> 00:14:32.410
Sir, isn't this enough?

00:14:33.360 --> 00:14:37.410
Kaito and the others are
sure to lose, aren't they?

00:14:37.410 --> 00:14:38.640
It's no use.

00:14:39.500 --> 00:14:40.690
Kaito.

00:14:41.390 --> 00:14:42.440
Can you hear me?

00:14:42.950 --> 00:14:44.790
Just give up already.

00:14:44.790 --> 00:14:47.360
If you accept defeat, all is forgiven.

00:14:47.360 --> 00:14:48.200
Isn't that ri-

00:14:54.430 --> 00:14:55.950
I won't stop.

00:14:57.330 --> 00:15:01.580
Don't tell me... this person really
plans to blow up the city!

00:15:01.990 --> 00:15:05.090
When it comes to puzzles,
lies are strictly forbidden.

00:15:08.510 --> 00:15:09.760
A baseball field?

00:15:10.410 --> 00:15:12.730
And baseball means diamond.

00:15:12.730 --> 00:15:15.820
A square diamond, so 4? No!

00:15:15.820 --> 00:15:17.830
A brilliant diamond has 58 facets, so 58.

00:15:17.830 --> 00:15:20.510
Ah! Baseball! Nine players, so 9!

00:15:20.510 --> 00:15:22.720
No way it's that simple!

00:15:22.720 --> 00:15:23.400
<i>Correct!</i>

00:15:23.400 --> 00:15:24.610
Huh?!
Yes!

00:15:25.750 --> 00:15:28.430
These are octagonal, so... 8, huh?

00:15:28.880 --> 00:15:32.240
<i>Correct! But hurry, there's little time.</i>

00:15:33.090 --> 00:15:35.930
Ah! A triangle-shaped
bench! So it's 3, right?

00:15:35.930 --> 00:15:37.170
It can't be that-

00:15:37.170 --> 00:15:38.880
Correct!<i>
What?!</i>

00:15:39.260 --> 00:15:40.120
Oh, there!

00:15:40.550 --> 00:15:42.130
It's a swan boat, so, 2!

00:15:42.560 --> 00:15:43.250
Correct!

00:15:43.720 --> 00:15:44.560
Yes!

00:15:44.560 --> 00:15:45.640
For real?

00:15:46.200 --> 00:15:48.350
<i>Still, even if we get all these numbers,</i>

00:15:48.350 --> 00:15:50.340
<i>with no hints about lining them up...</i>

00:15:50.770 --> 00:15:52.630
Three minutes left.

00:15:53.140 --> 00:15:55.100
This park is too big!

00:15:55.420 --> 00:15:57.980
This is hexagonal, so... 6.

00:15:58.410 --> 00:15:59.440
<i>Correct!</i>

00:16:01.120 --> 00:16:02.350
We won't make it.

00:16:03.490 --> 00:16:07.400
Thanks to you, they lost
some time at the beginning.

00:16:07.400 --> 00:16:09.570
They don't have enough left.

00:16:09.570 --> 00:16:11.450
Even if I hadn't done anything,

00:16:11.450 --> 00:16:14.200
this puzzle was unsolvable from the start, wasn't it?

00:16:14.900 --> 00:16:17.050
What was that?

00:16:17.050 --> 00:16:19.150
Sixteen minutes is too little time.

00:16:19.150 --> 00:16:21.340
There's no way they could explore the whole park.

00:16:21.340 --> 00:16:23.390
An unsolvable puzzle is meaningless.

00:16:23.390 --> 00:16:25.680
It can certainly be solved.

00:16:25.680 --> 00:16:28.300
Though, with only three
minutes now remaining,

00:16:28.300 --> 00:16:30.050
it may not be possible.

00:16:31.070 --> 00:16:33.590
Victory is mine!

00:16:34.050 --> 00:16:35.570
<i>Well, what shall you do?</i>

00:16:35.570 --> 00:16:37.840
<i>Start evacuating the
inhabitants now?</i>

00:16:37.840 --> 00:16:39.480
<i>Will you alone escape?</i>

00:16:39.480 --> 00:16:45.100
<i>Or will you choose to be blown to pieces
as miserable losers?</i>

00:16:48.020 --> 00:16:51.760
Dammit! Think, think! Think!

00:16:53.380 --> 00:16:55.360
Think! Think!

00:16:55.360 --> 00:16:57.370
Think!

00:17:00.170 --> 00:17:03.080
Kaito... You won't escape?

00:17:03.400 --> 00:17:05.620
From the start, there wasn't enough time

00:17:05.620 --> 00:17:07.040
to look for the numbers.

00:17:07.040 --> 00:17:12.100
Meaning, there must be another way
to fill those 16 blanks.

00:17:12.100 --> 00:17:14.810
How? What is the rule?

00:17:21.770 --> 00:17:23.270
Kaito!

00:17:32.160 --> 00:17:33.530
That eye again...

00:17:34.250 --> 00:17:35.070
How many minutes left?

00:17:36.340 --> 00:17:38.690
Um, 1 minute, 50 seconds.

00:17:38.690 --> 00:17:40.580
There's no time to solve the puzzle.

00:17:42.420 --> 00:17:43.290
Wait!

00:17:49.040 --> 00:17:50.470
Less than a minute!

00:17:50.470 --> 00:17:52.840
What will you do, Kaito?
Look for more numbers?

00:17:53.330 --> 00:17:54.380
No need.

00:17:54.420 --> 00:17:56.380
It seems he's noticed.

00:17:56.380 --> 00:17:59.140
Oh! These 16 blanks are...

00:17:59.370 --> 00:18:00.350
...a magic square?

00:18:00.350 --> 00:18:03.490
Yeah. The total for all rows, columns,
and diagonals is the same.

00:18:03.490 --> 00:18:04.640
That's a magic square.

00:18:05.370 --> 00:18:07.610
If there are 16 blanks,
the total must be 34,

00:18:07.610 --> 00:18:09.440
using numbers 1 through 16.

00:18:09.440 --> 00:18:11.150
That's why we don't have
to look for any more.

00:18:11.150 --> 00:18:13.420
But the numbers are all scattered.

00:18:13.420 --> 00:18:15.200
How should he line them up?

00:18:15.960 --> 00:18:17.490
Kaito! You have to escape!

00:18:18.020 --> 00:18:19.380
Kaito!

00:18:19.380 --> 00:18:20.470
Okay!

00:18:20.740 --> 00:18:23.230
I'll input the numbers, starting from 1!

00:18:23.230 --> 00:18:23.910
Move!

00:18:24.200 --> 00:18:27.310
What'd you say?! So, you get it?

00:18:27.760 --> 00:18:28.860
Like this.

00:18:33.310 --> 00:18:34.470
Oh!

00:18:34.880 --> 00:18:37.510
Still, only 20 seconds are left.

00:18:37.510 --> 00:18:39.520
He can't calculate that.

00:19:13.090 --> 00:19:15.710
I... lose?

00:19:16.330 --> 00:19:17.210
Impossible!

00:19:21.880 --> 00:19:23.390
Kaito...

00:19:26.370 --> 00:19:28.200
Good thing, huh, Kaito?

00:19:29.350 --> 00:19:32.520
Do you still not like that armlet,
though you used its power again?

00:19:33.010 --> 00:19:34.080
Where's the harm?

00:19:34.080 --> 00:19:35.860
Thanks to that, everyone was saved.

00:19:35.860 --> 00:19:39.640
It ain't thanks to this! It was MY skill!

00:19:39.640 --> 00:19:40.800
Yes, yes.

00:19:43.670 --> 00:19:46.120
Ah, Cubik! No thanks to you!

00:19:46.120 --> 00:19:47.910
I'm sorry, Kaito.

00:19:49.340 --> 00:19:51.950
Kaito, you were sort of cool.

00:19:51.950 --> 00:19:53.690
Wh..What the heck?

00:19:55.270 --> 00:19:57.280
I thought puzzles were worthless,

00:19:57.280 --> 00:19:59.340
but I can't take them from you.

00:20:02.340 --> 00:20:04.390
What was that power you used?

00:20:04.390 --> 00:20:06.060
Be my test subject and-

00:20:06.060 --> 00:20:08.720
More to the point, where's the prize,
huh? The PRIZE!

00:20:10.470 --> 00:20:11.480
Isn't that it?

00:20:18.730 --> 00:20:21.270
The city... It's sparkling.

00:20:21.270 --> 00:20:23.400
Yeah. It's pretty.

00:20:24.550 --> 00:20:27.330
So, there's no treasure?!

00:20:28.740 --> 00:20:32.330
If I were to blow them all up right now,

00:20:32.330 --> 00:20:34.980
my plan would be complete.

00:20:36.320 --> 00:20:38.320
I've endured the abuse of my superiors,

00:20:38.320 --> 00:20:40.540
the demands of my subordinates, all of it...

00:20:43.580 --> 00:20:45.340
And all for this day!

00:20:45.340 --> 00:20:47.930
Farewell, my city!

00:20:52.380 --> 00:20:53.350
Wh..Wha?

00:20:54.710 --> 00:20:56.600
Hello, Urban Development Unit.

00:20:57.970 --> 00:21:00.760
Oh, yes. Just a moment, please.

00:21:01.340 --> 00:21:04.130
Mr. Urban Development! Internal line 3.

00:21:04.130 --> 00:21:06.640
Ah. Thank you!

00:21:08.230 --> 00:21:11.090
Hello, how may I help you?

00:21:11.090 --> 00:21:12.530
I've removed the bomb.

00:21:13.330 --> 00:21:14.460
Bishop, sir!

00:21:15.200 --> 00:21:18.320
Trying to blow up the
city even though you lost

00:21:18.320 --> 00:21:20.490
to a Solver is conduct unbecoming a Giver.

00:21:20.490 --> 00:21:22.390
I revoke your Giver status.

00:21:23.930 --> 00:21:27.510
What?! Um, regarding that matter,

00:21:27.510 --> 00:21:29.160
if I could have one more chance...

00:21:29.160 --> 00:21:32.210
If you undertake any Giver
activities on your own,

00:21:32.210 --> 00:21:34.240
you will be neutralized.

00:21:34.240 --> 00:21:35.760
Please bear that in mind.

00:21:35.760 --> 00:21:36.290
Goodbye.

00:21:43.640 --> 00:21:47.180
Kaito Daimon is an
interesting person indeed.

00:21:51.680 --> 00:21:52.750
Kaito!

00:21:53.040 --> 00:21:55.090
Quit actin' like you're my frien-

00:21:55.700 --> 00:21:56.640
Good morning!

00:21:56.640 --> 00:21:58.330
G..Good morning.

00:22:00.480 --> 00:22:02.040
The heck is this?!

00:22:02.070 --> 00:22:05.320
I'm going to collect various
data on you, Kaito.

00:22:06.430 --> 00:22:08.110
Quit screwin' around! Get this offa me!

00:22:08.110 --> 00:22:10.460
Incidentally, if you
refuse, I can do THIS.

00:22:12.250 --> 00:22:17.870
Thanks to Kaito, Cubik appears to have
shown an interest in puzzles.

00:22:17.870 --> 00:22:22.480
Unforeseen chemical reactions
may well continue to occur, eh?

00:22:23.000 --> 00:22:25.280
If Kaito Daimon is involved.

00:22:36.840 --> 00:22:41.060
Tsukue no ue de umareta sekai
A world born on top of a desk

00:22:41.060 --> 00:22:46.980
Ichiban saki ni kimi ni misetakatta
I wanted to show it to you first of all

00:22:46.980 --> 00:22:51.610
Karappo no heya sotto nukedashite
I sneaked silently out of that empty room

00:22:51.610 --> 00:22:56.660
Hashirihajimeteta
And started running

00:22:57.820 --> 00:23:02.140
Iki hazumasete oka o noboru to
Breathing heavily, I climbed the hill

00:23:02.140 --> 00:23:07.500
Kimi ga saki ni tsuite matte ita ne
And you were already there, waiting

00:23:08.370 --> 00:23:12.680
Takusan no hajimete kimi to mitsuketa
There were so many treasures that I first

00:23:12.680 --> 00:23:17.930
Takaramono datta
Discovered with you

00:23:17.930 --> 00:23:23.270
Kanashisa de afureta toki wa
That time when I was overcome with sadness

00:23:23.270 --> 00:23:25.950
Nanimo iwazu ni tada
You said nothing

00:23:25.950 --> 00:23:28.860
Soba ni ite kureta ne
Just stayed there by my side, didn't you?

00:23:28.860 --> 00:23:33.430
Imademo wasurenai yo
Even now, I haven't forgotten

00:23:33.430 --> 00:23:38.730
Mata aou ne, yakusoku o shiyou
Let's meet again, let's make it a promise

00:23:38.730 --> 00:23:44.010
Kei wa shinai, ano hi no sayonara
It won't fade, the "goodbye" of that day

00:23:44.010 --> 00:23:49.550
Boku no subete, kimi ga kureta michi
Everything I have, the path you gave me

00:23:49.550 --> 00:23:58.490
Zutto kokoro no naka hikaru yo
Will always shine within my heart

00:24:03.540 --> 00:24:06.240
I'm tellin' ya, I don't need a partner!

00:24:06.240 --> 00:24:08.270
I solve puzzles on my own!

00:24:08.270 --> 00:24:11.220
I, Ana, know the emotions of pictures,

00:24:11.220 --> 00:24:13.810
so I think it's better to have me around.

00:24:13.810 --> 00:24:15.020
The emotions of pictures?

00:24:15.020 --> 00:24:17.060
Like happiness or sadness?

00:24:17.100 --> 00:24:18.680
Hm, maybe not.

00:24:18.680 --> 00:24:20.950
So, the feelings of the guy who drew it?

00:24:20.950 --> 00:24:22.390
Maybe not!

00:24:21.920 --> 00:24:27.130
The Girl in the Closed Room

00:24:22.390 --> 00:24:24.470
Next time: "The Girl in the Closed Room"

00:24:24.470 --> 00:24:26.400
We ain't a good match!
